/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 115 0 R
/T (A Multiplexer \(MUX\) is a basic combinational logic element that selects one signal from multiple inputs and passes it to a single output based on Selector inputs. The output is in a HIGH \(1\) state if the selected input is HIGH, while it is in a LOW \(0\) state if the selected input is LOW.)
/E (A Multiplexer \(MUX\) is a basic combinational logic element that selects one signal from multiple inputs and passes it to a single output based on Selector inputs. The output is in a HIGH \(1\) state if the selected input is HIGH, while it is in a LOW \(0\) state if the selected input is LOW.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
