/Title (A Multiplexer \(MUX\) is a basic combinational logic element that selects one signal from multiple inputs and passes it to a single output based on Selector inputs. The output is in a HIGH \(1\) state if the selected input is HIGH, while it is in a LOW \(0\) state if the selected input is LOW.)
